{
  "title": "Recognize catalog foods written with extra words, and fix Open Food Facts aisle quirks",
  "description": "Since the keyword rules were deleted (2026-10-20), a recipe or shopping line the catalog doesn't resolve gets its aisle from the AI name resolver on the server, else Open Food Facts, else Other. \
Offline, with no AI answers, that leaves 4,431 pipeline-fixture lines in Other that the keyword rules used to place (lines categorized 99.0% -> 91.8%); a spot check of them found mostly real foods the catalog misses because of extra words: prep words before the food ('finely-chopped fresh flat-leaf parsley', 'peeled and deveined shrimp', 'well-toasted cashews'), notes after it with no comma ('soy sauce preferably low sodium', 'Japanese yellow mustard if you wish'), brands ('Sargento Ricotta Cheese', 'Heinz chili sauce', 'Eagle sweetened condensed milk'), and leftover units ('Tbls extra virgin olive oil'). \
Each costs an AI call per name in prod and has no aisle until it's answered. \
Better name normalization in the catalog's resolver (dropping prep, size and brand words, and trailing notes) would recover many of these for calories and density too. \
Measure with make ingredient-catalog-audit (Lines categorized, Nutrition name recognized) and spot-check what moves. \n\
Open Food Facts quirks seen in the same check, each a wrong aisle where nothing else answers: butter variants ('sweet butter' -> Produce, 'garlic butter' and 'European-style butter' -> Oils & Vinegars), 'diced tomatoes with green chiles' -> Produce, pecans ('pecan chips', 'shelled pecans') -> Snacks, 'lemon pepper' -> Meat & Seafood, 'ginger juice' -> Beverages, 'fish stock' -> Spices & Seasonings, 'Seasonings' -> Condiments & Sauces, 'juniper berries' -> Condiments & Sauces. \
Most come from product-name or brand votes rather than the taxonomy; look for a systematic fix in scripts/import-open-food-facts.py or open_food_facts_aisles.json before adding catalog entries one by one. \
The shopping-list scorecard (make shopping-list-categorizer-test) reports wrong aisles apart from missing ones; its two wrong aisles are 'Dip' -> Cheese (Open Food Facts) and 'Ground flaxseed' -> Nuts & Dried Fruit (debatable label).",
